# CI workflow patterns (GitHub Actions & GitLab CI)

Narrows `core-common-rules`' design guidance to workflow-YAML structure and reuse. Applies only to GitHub Actions workflows under `.github/workflows/`, composite `action.yml`/`action.yaml` under `.github/actions/`, `.gitlab-ci.yml` and GitLab CI included config under `.gitlab/`, not to YAML the `docker-k8s-terraform` pack scopes.

## Trigger and concurrency shape

- Scope `on:`/`rules:` to the events needed (a branch, path filter or event type),
  not every push.
- Add a `concurrency:` group (GitHub Actions) or `resource_group` (GitLab CI) to
  any workflow that deploys or mutates shared state. Not `interruptible: true` for
  a deploy: it means the job is SAFE to auto-cancel, which fits a build/test job
  made obsolete by a newer commit, not a deploy in flight.
- Keep `pull_request` as the default trigger for anything that only builds or
  tests untrusted contributions; `pull_request_target` only when the job needs
  base-repo secrets, see `rules/security.mdc`.

## Job structure and reuse

- Give every job an explicit `name:` and a `timeout-minutes` (GitHub Actions) or
  job-level `timeout` (GitLab CI).
- Factor a step sequence used by more than one workflow into a reusable workflow
  (`workflow_call`) or composite action (GitHub Actions), or an
  `include:`/`extends:` template (GitLab CI).
- Pin `runs-on`/`image:` to a specific runner or image tag, not a rolling `latest`.
- Express real job dependencies with `needs:` (GitHub Actions) or
  `needs:`/stage ordering (GitLab CI), not implied default stage order.

## Caching and artifacts

- Key a cache (`actions/cache`, GitLab `cache:key`) off the lockfile or dependency
  manifest hash, not a static string.
- Scope `artifacts:`/`actions/upload-artifact` to the files a later job consumes,
  with an explicit retention/expiry, not a whole working directory.

## Anti-patterns to flag

- The same 10+ line step sequence duplicated across jobs or files instead of a
  reusable workflow, composite action or `include:`/`extends:` template.
- A job with no `timeout-minutes`/`timeout` on a step that can hang (a network
  call, a wait loop, an interactive prompt).
- A cache key that never changes (a literal string with no lockfile hash).
